--!strict
--[[
	Map themes: the same bases, belt and plaza in eight different worlds. Plain data only.

	A theme changes how the world looks, never how it plays: the plots, the belt, the walkway, the plaza and every
	gameplay position stay exactly where Config/Gameplay and Config/Scenery put them. What changes:
	  palette     Config/Theme.world colours of the scenery (ground, walkway, plaza, factory, trees, terrain, water...)
	  lighting    time of day, sky, haze and colour grading (same shape as Config/Scenery.lighting)
	  materials   the ground, the walkway and the boundary wall
	  flora       what grows on the tree spots (lollipops, palms, cacti, glowing mushrooms...)
	  landmarks   big props outside the wall (balloons, candy canes, ice spires, a volcano, a lighthouse...)
	  weather     particles drifting around each player (snow, embers, leaves, fireflies...; off with Reduce effects)

	A server starts on a random map (weighted) and changes map every `rotation.mapSeconds`: for the last
	`rotation.voteSeconds` everyone can vote for the next one from a few candidates (never the current map). A seasonal
	theme (Config/Seasons, e.g. Halloween) still adds its decorations, and its lighting wins over the map's while it runs.

	Studio: /map <id> switches now, /map vote starts a vote, /map list. Admins can use /map in live servers too (that
	server only). CI renders every map offline (tools/worldsim) and checks part budgets and colours
	(Logic/MapThemeRules.validate).
]]

